# Shell scripts run on the Linux host. A CRLF line ending in the shebang makes the
# kernel refuse the file with "bad interpreter", so keep these LF whatever the checkout
# platform does.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/systemd/* text eol=lf

# GeoNames name files are fixtures of a real download. countryInfo.txt is CRLF where the
# other two are LF, and the parser is tested against that, so git must not normalise it.
tests/fixtures/geonames/* -text
# -text on the whole directory, not just the CRLF one. Git was about to convert the two LF
# files to CRLF on a Windows checkout, which would have left every fixture in this directory
# CRLF and the LF half of the parser untested while the tests still passed.
